==Russian==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|ru|cu|съзьдати||to [[build]], to [[erect]]}} (1sg. {{m|cu|съзиждѫ}}). Not originally a compound of {{m|ru|дать}}, but later borrowed its conjugation from that verb. Compare also the corresponding older imperfective {{m|ru|созида́ть}}, with the same relationship as imperfective {{m|ru|-бира́ть}} to {{m|ru|брать}}. Synchronically derivable as {{m|ru|со-}} + {{m|ru||-здать}}, found only in this verb and derived from {{cog|orv|зьдати}} (1sg. {{m|orv|зижу}}). Cognate with {{cog|cu|зьдати||to [[build]], to [[erect]]}} (1sg. {{m|cu|зиждѫ}}), {{cog|bg|зи́дам||to [[build]], to [[construct]]}}, {{m|bg|зид||[[wall]]}}, {{cog|sh|зи́дати||to [[construct]] (from [[stone]]s)}} (1sg. {{m|sh|зи̑да̄м}}), {{m|sh|зи̑д||[[stone]] [[wall]]}} (gen. sg. {{m|sh|зи́ду}}), {{cog|sl|zídati||to [[build]] a [[wall]]}}, {{m|sl|zȋd||[[wall]]}}, {{cog|cs|zeď ||[[stone]] [[wall]]}} (gen. sg. {{m|cs|zdi}}), {{cog|pl|zdun||[[potter]]}}.

Per Vasmer, further cognate with {{cog|lt|žiẽsti||to [[mold]]}} (1sg. {{m|lt|žiedžiù}}, 1sg. past {{m|lt|žiedžiaũ}}), {{cog|lv|zìest||to [[smear]] with [[clay]]}}, {{cog|prg|seydis||[[wall]]}} and more distantly (with different vowels) with {{cog|lt|žaĩdas||[[oven]]}}, {{m|lt|židinỹs||[[hearth]]}}, {{cog|got|tr=deigan|||to [[knead]]}}, {{cog|sa|tr=dḗhmi|||to [[plaster]]}}, {{m|sa|tr=dēhī́|g=f|||[[shaft]], [[dam]], [[mound]]}}, {{cog|peo|tr=didā|||[[strengthening]]}} {{cog|grc|τεῖχος||[[stone]] [[wall]]}}, {{m|grc|τοῖχος||[[wall]]}}, {{cog|la|fingō||to [[shape]], to [[knead]]}} (infinitive {{m|la|fingere}}, supine {{m|la|fictum}}), {{cog|osc|féihúss||[[wall]]s {{i|acc. pl.}}}} {{cog|txh|-δίζος}}. The Balto-Slavic forms come from {{cog|ine-bsl-pro|*ǵheydh-}}, metathesis of {{cog|ine-pro|*dheyǵh-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|созда́ть}}
* {{audio|Ru-создать.ogg|Audio|lang=ru}}

===Verb===
{{ru-verb|созда́ть|pf|impf=создава́ть|impf2=созида́ть}}

# to [[create]]
# to [[found]], to [[originate]]
# to [[set up]], to [[establish]]
# {{lb|ru|literary}} to [[build]], to [[erect]]

====Usage notes====
* The imperfectives {{m|ru|создава́ть}} and {{m|ru|созида́ть}} have the same meaning, but the latter is literary or dated.

